. /etc/profile.d/001-functions

# 8 ms, which is as low as RetroArch goes: ask for less and it logs "raised
# to the minimum" and runs at 8 anyway. Upstream ships 32, and this was 24
# until the DSP stopped being what set the floor - #422 gave the period 10 ms
# at every rate instead of 480 frames, and #428 moved the playback graph to
# SH_MEM_PULL_MODE, so the DSP publishes a sample accurate position, the
# kernel stops setting SNDRV_PCM_INFO_BATCH and PipeWire stops keeping an
# extra period queued against a pointer that moved a period at a time.
#
# Swept downwards on the device to find a breaking point and there was none;
# pw-top's ERR stayed flat on Snes9x and SwanStation. pcm-flags reads the
# driver's own flags if this needs checking again.
#
# 8 was RetroArch's floor because its driver asked for a quantum of a
# quarter of the setting and floored that at 128 frames, and held the ring
# to two quanta: at 32 kHz both come to 256 frames, so asking for less was
# raised back. RetroArch patch 0017 and PipeWire's min-quantum both move to
# 64, so 4 is now a setting that means something - untested, which is why
# this still writes 8. docs/audio-latency.md.
AUDIO_LATENCY=$(get_setting audiolatency)
if [ -z "${AUDIO_LATENCY}" ]
then
  set_setting global.audiolatency 8
fi
